## Docker & Environment

### Docker Compose

`docker-compose.yml` at the **repository root** defines three services:

| Service | Image / build            | Port                    | Description                                        |
| ------------- | ------------------------ | ----------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |
| **budget-db** | `postgres:16-alpine`     | `5432` (localhost only) | PostgreSQL with health check                       |
| **budget-api** | `backend/Dockerfile`    | `8080` (localhost only) | .NET 10 API, waits for healthy DB                  |
| **budget-web** | `frontend/Dockerfile`   | `8081` (localhost only) | Static SPA (Vite build), waits for healthy API     |

The API container runs as a non-root user for security.

### Environment Variables

**Local development:** no env files are required—`docker-compose.yml` defaults cover the API/DB, and the frontend Docker build uses committed `frontend/.env`. **Overrides:** optional root `.env`, `backend/.env.production`, and/or `frontend/.env.production` (Compose reads root `.env`; `./run-server.sh` sources those when present). Templates: `backend/.env.production.template`, `frontend/.env.production.template`; for Vite dev without the committed `.env`, copy `frontend/env.template` → `frontend/.env`.

| Variable                 | Default            | Description                             |
| ------------------------ | ------------------ | --------------------------------------- |
| `JWT_SECRET_KEY`         | _(template value)_ | JWT signing key (minimum 32 characters) |
| `BUDGET_USER`            | `admin`            | Default seeded user username            |
| `BUDGET_PASSWORD`        | `admin`            | Default seeded user password            |
| `DB_HOST`                | `budget-db`        | Database host (Docker service name)     |
| `DB_PORT`                | `5432`             | Database port                           |
| `DB_NAME`                | `budget-sqldb`     | Database name                           |
| `DB_USER`                | `postgres`         | Database user                           |
| `DB_PASSWORD`            | `postgrespw`       | Database password                       |
| `ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT` | `Production`       | ASP.NET environment                     |
| `VITE_API_URL`           | _(frontend template)_ | Browser-reachable API URL (web build) |
| `VITE_LIST_PAGE_SIZE`    | `10`               | Default list page size (frontend)       |

### Health Check

The API exposes a health endpoint at `GET /health` returning `{ status: "Healthy", timestamp: "..." }`.

